==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|у-|лови́ть}}.

Masculine past form {{m|ru|уловил}} had in Middle Russian stress on the first vowel, while feminine past {{m|ru|уловила}} had stress on the last vowel. In modern speech, both the masculine and feminine past have stress on the third vowel. Similar process has happened to {{m|ru|помянуть}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|улови́ть}}
